   Now then. Here's a few recommendations from me (as well as;
addressing some popular questions)...


   - Please. Do not post any; game secrets, spoilers, and/or related
material in this thread. Read the prologues in the above links as to
the reason why. Tips on how to work the game controls, and/or about
the game commands though, are welcome.


   - Read the story slow. Don't rush through it. Else you may get
somewhat confused. Well, I do - and I'm the one that should understand
it the most (laugh!). My writing style changes and/or evolves as I
progress through the story. That's cause I'm now much more comfortable
with; my character (Ellora), the game, how it behaves, and my own
insecurities concerning my lack of compositional ability, then when I
first started writing about it.


   - I have no formal skills in writing or composition. Some sentences
(lines in the story); are what the computer (the game) gives me.
Others; are what's going through my mind. Yet others are; what's
transpiring on the screen, or how I interpret what's happening, while
I play. And still others are; what I imagine that my character would
be saying / thinking. So then: They can be whatever (laugh)! There's
no pattern. I fluctuate back and forth, while drifting in and out, as
my moods ebb and flow...


   - You'll see questions spread throughout the different parts of the
story. That's just me, or my character, talking to myself. It gives
you (the reader) an idea of what's going through my mind, sometimes...


   - Each "Part" of the story should be considered, or thought of, as
a chapter. I originally was just doing it to show some people how I
got to a certain point in the game. I didn't know that Google allowed
only so many letters (what I call characters) per post. So I was just
going to string them, one after the other, in one thread. Thereby
creating one long post with different parts to it. But, much to my
surprise at the time, people started posting in the thread. So my idea
didn't work out (laugh!). That's why I called them "Parts" in the
beginning. In subsequent posts, I just kept up the same naming
nomenclature, in order to lessen any confusion.


   - Each major thread (there are presently two major ones), should be
viewed as a book. The major threads contain the posts by me, with the
different parts. The minor ones are like sidetracks and/or holding
patterns. This one will (hopefully) be the third major thread
involving the story. Hence "Book 3".


