   - As I play the game, I jot down some notes. Then when I come to
the end of a session, I make a general outline. Over the next few
days, I flesh it out. A session can last anywhere from one night, to
whenever (some were over the span of a few weeks). This all depends on
how much time I have in the real world. I do try to have a theme
within each Part (chapter), though.


   - Ellora (our heroine in the Saga), is loosely based on two things:

    On the 'archer' sub class, of the 'fighter' character class, from
AD&D (circa early '80's).

    And one of the heroes (Allora The Elven Archer), that appeared in
a game called "Master of Magic". There aren't many sites left to that
old game on the internet anymore. It only worked in DOS, that's if
your old enough to know what that means (wink). Here's the best I
could find on her from what's left out there.

    http://mom.diaspora.ru/txt/heroes.doc/Document/allora.html

    The prologue in the first story thread has additional information
on what I had intended.


   - Will I write / compose another story? 

